<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<wodefinitions>
	<wo class="ERXWOForm" content="expected" unknownAttributes="passthrough">

		<doc><![CDATA[Renders a `<form>`. Installed in place of `WOForm`, so it's what `<wo:form>` and `WOForm` render. Submits to its `action`, a direct action (`directActionName`/`actionClass`) or an `href`; without any of them, to the page's component action URL, where the submitted buttons decide the action. The method is `post` unless bound. As in WO's, a form inside another form is left out (browsers don't support nested forms), and an off-screen default submit button can be added (`addDefaultSubmitButton`), so pressing return submits. Differences from WO's:

- A nested form is left out with a logged warning, and not at all when it's `embedded`.
- Every form has a name, generated when `name` isn't bound (WO names only forms with a bound `name`), and publishes it to the context, for elements that need to refer to their form.
- `disabled` leaves the form's tags out, and `fragmentIdentifier` appends `#` + its value to the action.

Attributes prefixed with `?` become query parameters. Every other attribute is rendered on the tag.]]></doc>

		<binding name="action"><pull><type>com.webobjects.appserver.WOActionResults</type></pull><doc>Component action invoked on submit. Must not be a constant.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="directActionName"><pull><type>java.lang.String</type></pull><doc>Direct action to submit to (in `actionClass`, or `DirectAction`).</doc></binding>
		<binding name="actionClass"><pull><type>java.lang.String</type></pull><doc>Direct action class.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="href"><pull><type>java.lang.String</type></pull><doc>URL to submit to.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="queryDictionary"><pull><type>java.util.Map</type></pull><doc>Query parameters added to the form's URL.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="fragmentIdentifier"><pull><type>java.lang.String</type></pull><doc>Fragment (`#…`) appended to the form's URL, for example to scroll to error messages after submitting.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="secure"><pull><type>java.lang.Boolean</type></pull><doc>Submit to an https URL.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="method"><pull><type>java.lang.String</type></pull><doc>The HTTP method. Defaults to `post`.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="enctype"><pull><type>java.lang.String</type></pull><doc>The form's encoding. A file upload inside the form requires `multipart/form-data`.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="name"><pull><type>java.lang.String</type></pull><doc>The form's name, also published to the context for elements inside it.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="id"><pull><type>java.lang.String</type></pull><doc>The form's `id`. With `er.extensions.ERXWOForm.useIdInsteadOfNameTag`, used as the form's name, rendered as `id`.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="multipleSubmit"><pull><type>java.lang.Boolean</type></pull><doc>Whether the form has several submit buttons, each with its own action. Defaults to `er.extensions.ERXWOForm.multipleSubmitDefault`.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="addDefaultSubmitButton"><pull><type>java.lang.Boolean</type></pull><doc>Add an off-screen submit button at the start of the form, so pressing return submits it. Defaults to `er.extensions.ERXWOForm.addDefaultSubmitButtonDefault`.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="disabled"><pull><type>java.lang.Boolean</type></pull><doc>If true, the form's tags are left out and only its content renders.</doc></binding>
		<binding name="embedded"><pull><type>java.lang.Boolean</type></pull><doc>Render the form even inside another form, for forms that are nested in the markup but independent for the user, such as in a modal container.</doc></binding>

		<choose max="1">
			<binding name="action"/>
			<binding name="href"/>
			<any-of><binding name="directActionName"/><binding name="actionClass"/></any-of>
		</choose>
		<requires binding="action" must="gettable"/>

	</wo>
</wodefinitions>
